Proposal (lane RELEASE, C9 (a)): a hosted job on free-threaded CPython 3.14.

Not applied: .github/workflows/ and tools/ are frozen; only Lucas applies this, by
his hand or his word. Apply from the repository root, after the change that adds
tools/release/requirements-ci-314t.txt is on the branch:

    git apply --check tools/release/proposals/ci-314t.patch
    git apply tools/release/proposals/ci-314t.patch

What it does:
- .github/workflows/ci.yml: a job core-314t ("core 3.14t") on ubuntu-24.04, allocated
  exactly like linux-tests (same if:), that installs cryptography from the
  hash-locked tools/release/requirements-ci-314t.txt, checks that the interpreter is
  free-threaded with the GIL off, and runs
      PYTHONPATH=core python -X gil=0 -B -m unittest discover -s core -t core
  with TMPDIR in a fresh folder under /tmp (outside /home/runner) and
  XDG_RUNTIME_DIR in a fresh folder under /dev/shm, the session bus unset.
  The required linux shell needs core-314t to succeed on full scope and to be
  skipped on docs-only scope, as it already does for linux-tests.
- tools/test_ci_scheduling.py: the workflow-shape, if: oracle and fail-closed
  matrices taught the new job and the new input of the linux shell.

Blank context lines are written as empty lines, which git apply accepts; the file
then has no trailing whitespace for the gate's whitespace check.

